## 7. Security and Access Control Design

The system design includes a proposed security model centred on role-based access control and secure session management.

### 7.1 Roles

| Role | Primary Responsibilities |
|---|---|
| Shop Owner / Manager | Access retail data, dashboards, forecasting, recommendations, and AI assistant features |
| Administrator | Manage user accounts, roles, and system-level administration |

### 7.2 Security objectives

The system should:

- authenticate users before allowing access to protected features
- restrict access by role and permission
- prevent privilege escalation
- protect business data from unauthorised access
- ensure AI-assisted access follows the same user permissions
- record security-relevant events for accountability
- enforce access checks on the backend, not only in the UI

### 7.3 Security design summary

The security design confirms that:

- credentials must be protected
- sessions must be time-limited and invalidated on logout
- backend checks must enforce authorisation
- data must not be exposed to users without permission
- AI assistant access must respect the same access model
- audit logging should be used for privileged and failed operations

This design is compatible with the repository’s M06-05 design document and provides the required security basis for the system.

